@rasmith it was suggested by [Gemini](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43212#discussion_r3274227503).

> simply returning from this async function without an await can cause this client's coroutine to monopolize the event loop, especially if requests are consistently slow.

I don't have much experience with async programming, so it is hard to say whether it is strictly necessary or not.

